{
  "_about": "How each spell looks: its own cast animation (`anim`, a pose in game/entities/rig.gd) and its own effects, played when the spell goes (`cast`, at you) and where it lands (`impact`, at the target, or at you for a sweep or burst). Linked to data/abilities.json by spell id; a spell missing here keeps its kind's generic animation and effect. Each effect part has `fx`: `mesh` (a shape from assets/models/fx, built by assets/blender/build_fx.py), `ring` (flat shockwave), `sparks`, `dust`, `flash` or `shake`. Mesh parts take `mesh`, `colour` (default: the spell's school), `glow` (brightness), `life` (seconds, or a tuning key such as `window`), `delay`, `size` [start, end] (scale over the life), `scale` [x, y, z], `height` and `forward` (metres from the anchor along the facing; negative is back toward you at a target), `rot` [x, y, z] degrees, `faceCamera` (an upright shape turns to face the fixed camera, so it never shows side on; `angle` then tilts it on screen, and it mirrors when you face screen left), `spin` (degrees the shape turns about its own axis over its life, which sells a swing), `follow` (stays on you) and `whileBraced` (shown only while a guard is up). Besides `cast` and `impact`, `windup` plays on you while a cast is drawn out (a cast-time spell or a channel; `life` \"castTime\" lasts it out) and `projectile` lists shapes carried by the spell's bolt or arrow (`mesh`, `colour`, `glow`, `scale`, `forward`). A mesh part's `fall` drops it from that many metres above onto its place (Light's Hammer). `windupAnim` is the pose held through a cast, `anim` the one played as it goes. `anim` takes `type`, `duration` (seconds, or a tuning key) and `impact` (0..1, when the blow lands); sweeps, bursts and charges keep their own timing so the blow and the pose stay together. The full list of planned looks for every spell is docs/spell-effects.md.",
